Pasal 4
Pelembagaan PUG meliputi:
a. penetapan koordinator PUG;
b. pokja PUG;
c. Focal Point PUG;
d. Penganggaran;
e. perencanaan pembangunan berbasis g ender;
f. pemantauan dan evaluasi;
g. pelaporan; dan
h. pengawasan.

translated_text:
Article 4
The institutionalization of PUG includes:
a. appointment of PUG coordinator;
b. PUG working group;
c. PUG Focal Point;
d. Budgeting;
e. gender-based development planning;
f. monitoring and evaluation;
g. reporting; and
h. supervision.

Article 6
(1) The Regent has the authority to establish the PUG Working Group.
(2) The establishment of the PUG Working Group as referred to in paragraph (1) shall be stipulated by a Regent’s Decree.
(3) The Regent’s Decree as referred to in paragraph (2) shall be valid for 5 (five) years.
(4) The management of the PUG Working Group consists of:
a. chairperson, headed by the head of the agency;
b. secretariat, served by the head of the department (dinas);
c. members comprising:
1. heads of PD;
2. a technical team consisting of:
a) officials who have attended training or education in gender-responsive budget analysis, a maximum of 5 (five) persons;
b) representatives from higher education institutions, a maximum of 5 (five) persons;
c) press representatives, a maximum of 5 (five) persons; and
d) representatives from non-governmental organizations whose scope of orientation is in the field of gender, a maximum of 5 (five) persons.

text:
Pasal 7
Tugas Pokja PUG meliputi:
a. mempromosikan dan memfasilitasi dialog antar unit kerja lingkup  pemerintahan daerah;
b. mengembangkan jaringan kerja sesuai dengan tugas pokok, fungsi  dan kewenangan yang diberikan oleh pimpinan dalam upaya  mewujudkan kesetaraan dan keadilan gender;
c. menugaskan tim teknis untuk melakukan penyusunan RAD PUG  dalam rangka mewujudkan kesetaraan dan keadilan gender yang  disesuaikan dengan periodisasi RPJMD;
d. menjabarkan dan menindaklanjuti kebijakan dan program  pelaksanaan agar responsif gender yang tersirat dan tersurat  dalam RPJMD;
e. mengkoordinasikan pembentukan Focal Point PUG di setiap PD  atau unit kerja;
f. mempromosikan PUG ditiap PD;
g. melakukan penguatan kapasitas bagi para Focal Point PUG dalam  menyusun anggaran yang responsif gender oleh tim teknis; h. mengawal penyusunan perencanaan dan anggaran responsif  gender di PD masing-masing;
i. memasukan indikator gender dalam pedoman penyusunan APBD; j. memastikan anggaran responsif gender menjadi pertimbangan  dalam pembahasan dan penetapan APBD bersama DPRD; k. mengadakan rapat koordinasi setiap 6 (enam) bulan sekali untuk  memastikan pelaksanaan PUG di Daerah;
l. membuat dan menyampaikan laporan pelaksanaan PUG kepada  bupati setiap 6 (enam) bulan; dan
m. mengadakan rapat koordinasi sebelum penyusunan RKPD.

translated_text:
Article 7
The duties of the PUG Working Group include:
a. promoting and facilitating dialogue among work units within the scope of regional government;
b. developing work networks in accordance with the main duties, functions and authorities granted by leadership in efforts to realize gender equality and justice;
c. assigning technical teams to carry out the preparation of the PUG RAD in order to realize gender equality and justice adjusted to the RPJMD periodization;
d. elaborating and following up on policies and implementation programs to be gender responsive both implicitly and explicitly stated in the RPJMD;
e. coordinating the establishment of PUG Focal Points in every PD or work unit;
f. promoting PUG in every PD;
g. conducting capacity strengthening for PUG Focal Points in preparing gender responsive budgets by the technical team;
h. overseeing the preparation of gender responsive planning and budgets in respective PDs;
i. incorporating gender indicators in the guidelines for preparing the APBD;
j. ensuring gender responsive budgets become a consideration in the discussion and determination of the APBD together with the DPRD;
k. holding coordination meetings every 6 (six) months to ensure the implementation of PUG in the Region;
l. preparing and submitting reports on PUG implementation to the regent every 6 (six) months; and
m. holding coordination meetings before the preparation of the RKPD.

text:
Pasal 12
Tugas Focal Point PUG meliputi:
a. membantu pengambil kebijakan unit kerja dalam ruang lingkup  tugas, pokok dan fungsi instansinya untuk secara terencana  mengambil langkah sepenuhnya apabila terdapat kesenjangan gender;
b. mendorong dan membantu unit kerja untuk mengevaluasi dan  memperbaiki mandat, kebijakan, program, proyek, kegiatan dan  anggaran agar lebih responsif gender;
c. memfasilitasi pelaksanaan pelatihan sensitifitas gender,  pelatihan analisis gender dan mengembangkan jaringan kerja  gender dengan instansi atau lembaga atau organisasi dan unit  kerja lainnya, baik pemerintah maupun non pemerintah;
d. mengupayakan terselenggaranya analisis gender sebagai salah  satu tahap di dalam setiap proses pembangunan yang dimulai  dari tahap perencanaan, pelaksanaan, pemantauan dan evaluasi;
e. menjabarkan dan menindaklanjuti kebijakan dan program  pelaksanaan pembangunan agar responsif gender yang tersirat  dalam Renstra PD,Renja PD dan RKPD;
f. ikut serta dalam berbagai kegiatan yang diselenggarakan oleh  Pokja PUG dan/atau kelompok kerja nasional PUG; dan g. membuat laporan kegiatan secara periodik dan dilaporkan  kepada bupati melalui ketua pokja PUG.

translated_text:
Article 12
The duties of the PUG Focal Point include:
a. assisting policy makers of work units within the scope of duties, principal tasks and functions of their agencies to take planned steps fully when there are gender gaps;
b. encouraging and assisting work units to evaluate and improve mandates, policies, programs, projects, activities and budgets to be more gender responsive;
c. facilitating the implementation of gender sensitivity training, gender analysis training and developing gender work networks with agencies or institutions or organizations and other work units, both government and non-government;
d. endeavoring to ensure the implementation of gender analysis as one of the stages in every development process starting from the planning, implementation, monitoring and evaluation stages;
e. elaborating and following up on policies and programs for development implementation to be gender responsive as implied in the PD Strategic Plan, PD Work Plan and RKPD;
f. participating in various activities organized by the PUG Working Group and/or the national PUG working group; and
g. preparing activity reports periodically and reporting them to the Regent through the chairperson of the PUG working group.

text:
Pasal 13
(1) Pemerintah Daerah bertanggungjawab menyusun perencanaan  kebijakan, program dan kegiatan pembangunan berperspektif Gender.
(2) Tanggung jawab sebagaimana dimaksud pada ayat (1)  dikoordinasikan oleh PD yang menyelenggarakan urusan  pemerintahan di bidang perencanaan pembangunan, penelitian  dan pengembangan Daerah.
(3) Perencanaan sebagaimana dimaksud pada ayat (1) meliputi tahapan:
a. Musrenbangdus;
b. Musrembangdes/kel;
c. Musrembangcam;
d. Musrenbang tingkat daerah;
e. penyusunan RPJMD;
f. penyusunan Renstra PD;
g. penyusunan Renja PD; dan
h. RKPD;
i. penyusunan RAPBD;
(4) Perencanaan sebagaimana dimaksud pada ayat (1) dilakukan  melalui analisis Gender dengan menggunakan metode Gender  Analisys Pathway atau metode analisis lain.
(5) Pelaksanaan analisis Gender terhadap RPJMD dan Renstra PD  dapat bekerjasama dengan lembaga Perguruan Tinggi atau pihak  lain yang memiliki kapabilitas di bidangnya.

translated_text:
Article 13
(1) Regional Government is responsible for formulating planning of policies, programs and activities for Gender-responsive development.
(2) The responsibility as referred to in paragraph (1) shall be coordinated by the Regional Apparatus that administers governmental affairs in the field of development planning, regional research and development.
(3) Planning as referred to in paragraph (1) includes the stages of:
a. Musrenbangdus;
b. Musrembangdes/kel;
c. Musrembangcam;
d. Musrenbang at regional level;
e. formulation of RPJMD;
f. formulation of Regional Apparatus Strategic Plan;
g. formulation of Regional Apparatus Work Plan; and
h. RKPD;
i. formulation of RAPBD;
(4) Planning as referred to in paragraph (1) shall be conducted through Gender analysis using the Gender Analysis Pathway method or other analytical methods.
(5) Implementation of Gender analysis on RPJMD and Regional Apparatus Strategic Plan may cooperate with Higher Education institutions or other parties that have capability in their field.

text:
Pasal 14
(1) Badan bertanggung jawab menyusun panduan perencanaan  pembangunan berbasis gender.
(2) Panduan sebagaimana dimaksud pada ayat (1) harus digunakan  dalam memfasilitasi:
a. Musrenbangdus;
b. Musrembangdes/kel;
c. Musrembangcam;
d. Musrenbang tingkat daerah;
e. penyusunan RPJMD;
f. penyusunan Renstra PD; dan
g. penyusunan Renja PD, yang responsif gender.
(3) Penyusunan panduan sebagaimana dimaksud pada ayat  (1)dapat bekerja sama dengan Tim Teknis Pokja PUG.

translated_text:
Article 14
(1) The Agency is responsible for preparing guidelines for gender-based development planning.
(2) The guidelines as referred to in paragraph (1) must be used in facilitating:
a. Musrenbangdus;
b. Musrembangdes/kel;
c. Musrembangcam;
d. Musrenbang at the regional level;
e. preparation of RPJMD;
f. preparation of Renstra PD; and
g. preparation of Renja PD, that is gender responsive.
(3) The preparation of guidelines as referred to in paragraph (1) may collaborate with the Technical Team of Pokja PUG.

text:
Pasal 15
(1) Metode Gender Analisys Pathway sebagaimana dimaksud dalam Pasal 13 ayat (4) digunakan sebagai cara membuat perencanaan di setiap PD.
(2) Metode sebagaimana dimaksud pada ayat (1) meliputi: a. tahap I analisa kebijakan yang responsif gender;
b. tahap II formulasi kebijakan yang responsif gender; c. tahap III rencana aksi yang responsif gender;
d. tahap IV pelaksanaan kegiatan yang sudah disusun; dan e. tahap V monitoring dan evaluasi dari setiap tahap dan  langkah yang diambil.

translated_text:
Article 15
(1) The Gender Analysis Pathway method as referred to in Article 13 paragraph (4) is used as a way to make planning in every PD.
(2) The method as referred to in paragraph (1) includes: a. stage I analysis of gender responsive policies;
b. stage II formulation of gender responsive policies; c. stage III gender responsive action plan;
d. stage IV implementation of activities that have been prepared; and e. stage V monitoring and evaluation of every stage and step taken.

Article 19
Evaluation of PUG implementation is conducted through:
a. evaluation of achievements and challenges in the implementation of RAD PUG;
b. preparation of RAD PUG for the next period;
c. evaluation of achievements and challenges in PUG implementation every 6 (six) months; and
d. preparation of the PUG implementation plan for the next 6 (six) months.

text:
Pasal 27
(1) PD yang menyelenggarakan urusan pemerintahan di bidang  sosial bertanggungjawab dalam memfasilitasi Pemberdayaan  Perempuan di bidang sosial budaya.
(2) Pemberdayaan Perempuan di bidang sosial budaya melalui: a. peningkatan pengetahuan, sikap dan keterampilan untuk  mendorong pemenuhan pendidikan secara berjenjang sesuai  dengan potensi untuk meningkatkan status sosial;
b. peningkatan kesadaran, kemauan dan kemampuan untuk  mengatasipermasalahan kesehatan melalui upaya promotif,  preventif, kuratif, dan rehabilitatif yang berkualitas  utamanya di bidang kesehatan reproduksi;
c. peningkatan kesadaran dan pengetahuan tentang  perencanaan keluarga mandiri, sehat dan sejahtera  termasuk akses layanan konsultasi dan pencatatan  perkawinan; dan
d. fasilitasi dan upaya pelestarian adat istiadat dan  pengembangan ilmu pengetahuan, teknologi, seni dan  budaya untuk kemajuan perempuan.

translated_text:
Article 27
(1) PD that administers governmental affairs in the social sector is responsible for facilitating Women's Empowerment in the socio-cultural sector.
(2) Women's Empowerment in the socio-cultural sector through: a. enhancement of knowledge, attitudes and skills to encourage the fulfillment of tiered education in accordance with potential to improve social status;
b. enhancement of awareness, willingness and ability to address health problems through quality promotive, preventive, curative, and rehabilitative efforts primarily in the field of reproductive health;
c. enhancement of awareness and knowledge about independent, healthy and prosperous family planning including access to consultation services and marriage registration; and
d. facilitation and efforts to preserve customs and traditions and development of science, technology, arts and culture for the advancement of women.

Article 28
(1) PD that administers governmental affairs in the field of cooperatives, small and medium enterprises and industry and trade is responsible for facilitating Women's Empowerment in the economic field.
(2) The implementation of Women's Empowerment in the economic field is carried out through:
a. provision of skills and job training;
b. facilitation of the formation of productive economic business groups;
c. facilitation of strengthening and development of productive economic business groups;
d. facilitation and capital assistance; and
e. facilitation of marketing network development.

text:
Pasal 30
Perlindungan Perempuan meliputi :
a. penguatan dan pengembangan lembaga penyedia layanan  perlindungan perempuan;
b. pencegahan kekerasan terhadap perempuan;dan c. penguatan dan pengembangan lembaga penyedia layanan  perlindungan perempuan korban kekerasan;

translated_text:
Article 30
Protection of Women includes:
a. strengthening and development of institutions providing women's protection services;
b. prevention of violence against women; and
c. strengthening and development of institutions providing protection services for women victims of violence;

text:
Pasal 32
(1) Penyusunanan RAD sebagaimana dimaksud dalam Pasal 7  huruf c dilaksanakan melalui mekanisme:
a. penetapan tim penyusun;
b. melakukan rapat untuk membentuk kelompok kerja  berdasarkan indikator;
c. setiap Pokja melakukan identifikasi tujuan, target dan indikator;
d. menetapkan program dan kegiatan prioritas terkait  pencapaian masing- masing target; dan
e. menetapkan alokasi anggaran setiap program kegiatan. (2) RAD paling sedikit memuat:
a. pendahuluan;
b. arah kebijakan dan strategi pencapaian;
c. pemantauan dan evaluasi;
d. penutup;dan
e. lampiran yang berisi matriks pelaksanaan RAD. (3) Penyusunan RAD dilaksanakan dengan memperhatikan: a. RPJMN;
b. RPJMD; dan
c. dokumen terkait lainnya.
(4) Ketentuan mengenai pelaksanaan RAD diatur lebih lanjut dengan Peraturan Bupati.

translated_text:
Article 32
(1) The preparation of RAD as referred to in Article 7 letter c is implemented through the following mechanism:
a. establishment of a drafting team;
b. conducting meetings to form working groups based on indicators;
c. each Working Group (Pokja) conducts identification of objectives, targets, and indicators;
d. determining priority programs and activities related to the achievement of each target; and
e. determining the budget allocation for each program/activity.
(2) RAD shall contain at minimum:
a. introduction;
b. policy direction and achievement strategy;
c. monitoring and evaluation;
d. closing; and
e. an appendix containing the RAD implementation matrix.
(3) The preparation of RAD is implemented with due regard to:
a. RPJMN;
b. RPJMD; and
c. other related documents.
(4) Provisions regarding the implementation of RAD shall be further regulated by a Regent Regulation.

Article 35
(1) The Agency is responsible for implementing efforts to prevent the occurrence of Violence against Women.
(2) Prevention as referred to in paragraph (1) is implemented in the form of:
a. conducting counseling and socialization regarding matters related to violence against women;
b. conducting socialization on women's rights;
c. endeavoring to improve education for women;
d. providing counseling to immediately report to local authorities if Violence against women occurs;
e. empowering social community organizations and women's organizations to increase women's knowledge and insight; and
f. establishing a network in the context of efforts to prevent violence against women.

text:
Pasal 39
(1) Fasilitasi pembentukan lembaga penyedia layanan sebagaimana  dimaksud dalam Pasal 36 ayat (2) huruf a dilaksanakan dengan  cara membentuk pusat pembelajaran keluarga.
(2) Tahapan pembentukan pusat pembelajaran keluarga meliputi: a. menyiapkan regulasi;
b. menyiapkan sumberdaya manusia;
c. menyiapkan sarana dan prasarana; dan
d. pembentukan pusat pembelajaran keluarga.
(3) Pusat pembelajaran keluarga berfungsi:
a. sebagai lembaga layanan dalam pencegahan dan konseling; b. sebagai tempat penghubung rujukan sebagai solusi bagi  permasalahan anak dan keluarga;
c. penguatan kemampuan keluarga dalam mengasuh dan  melindungi anak;
d. sebagai tempat pembelajaran keluarga melalui pendidikan bagi  orang tua; dan
e. sebagai layanan satu pintu keluarga holistik integratif  berbasis hak anak.

translated_text:
Article 39
(1) Facilitation of the establishment of service provider institutions as referred to in Article 36 paragraph (2) letter a is implemented by establishing family learning centers.
(2) The stages of establishing family learning centers include:
 a. preparing regulations;
 b. preparing human resources;
 c. preparing facilities and infrastructure; and
 d. establishment of family learning centers.
(3) Family learning centers function:
 a. as service institutions in prevention and counseling;
 b. as a referral liaison point as a solution for child and family problems;
 c. strengthening family capacity in nurturing and protecting children;
 d. as a place for family learning through education for parents; and
 e. as a one-stop holistic integrative family service based on children's rights.
